1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,247
Most people who need to change a project
were never taught Git.

2
00:00:04,247 --> 00:00:09,503
Gangplank puts them on a branch of their
own, in a browser, checks what they save,

3
00:00:09,503 --> 00:00:12,748
and hands the work to the team as a
review request.

4
00:00:12,748 --> 00:00:14,652
The shared branch never moves.

5
00:00:14,652 --> 00:00:16,234
Gangplank runs on your PC.

6
00:00:16,234 --> 00:00:21,795
A PowerShell server listens on localhost,
your browser is the interface,

7
00:00:21,795 --> 00:00:25,398
and nothing like git,
Node or Python is needed.

8
00:00:26,098 --> 00:00:30,855
Inside the server: Smart Save,
the Sentinel secret scan,

9
00:00:30,855 --> 00:00:32,325
and an audit log.

10
00:00:32,325 --> 00:00:35,083
You edit files in an ordinary folder.

11
00:00:35,783 --> 00:00:39,838
Out to GitHub or GitLab over HTTPS,
on a branch of your own.

12
00:00:39,838 --> 00:00:43,604
AI help goes through Fairlead only.

13
00:00:43,604 --> 00:00:47,855
Lazarette, the vault,
is an opt-in source for Git tokens.

14
00:00:48,555 --> 00:00:54,140
Safe by design: your branch only,
stop if it moved, secrets blocked,

15
00:00:54,140 --> 00:00:55,807
every write audited.

16
00:00:55,807 --> 00:01:00,360
Single sign-on and roles are planned,
not built.

17
00:01:00,964 --> 00:01:02,990
Setup starts in Fairlead.

18
00:01:02,990 --> 00:01:07,317
One click installs a key for Gangplank in
Windows Credential Manager.

19
00:01:07,317 --> 00:01:11,750
The key is never shown,
and Gangplank reads it from there.

20
00:01:11,988 --> 00:01:12,988
Then launch.

21
00:01:12,988 --> 00:01:16,663
A local server starts and your browser
gets a one-time link.

22
00:01:16,663 --> 00:01:20,771
This is the test-mode launcher,
so the GitHub behind it is synthetic and

23
00:01:20,771 --> 00:01:21,771
Lazarette is off.

24
00:01:22,005 --> 00:01:27,656
The job: a watchstander must add weekend
maintenance notes to the team project.

25
00:01:27,656 --> 00:01:32,802
Paste the address, connect, name a branch,

26
00:01:32,802 --> 00:01:34,027
and start.

27
00:01:34,727 --> 00:01:38,219
Gangplank downloads a fresh copy to a
folder of their own.

28
00:01:38,219 --> 00:01:42,714
They edit with ordinary tools: the notes,
a readme line,

29
00:01:42,714 --> 00:01:47,127
and by mistake an old deploy script
with a token in it.

30
00:01:47,827 --> 00:01:49,649
Smart Save lists what changed.

31
00:01:49,649 --> 00:01:53,886
The script with the token is
excluded automatically,

32
00:01:53,886 --> 00:01:58,870
and the Sentinel scan names it:
a possible GitHub credential.

33
00:01:59,570 --> 00:02:03,522
For the commit title,
Refine using AI asks first.

34
00:02:03,522 --> 00:02:06,989
Only file names and change types go out,

35
00:02:06,989 --> 00:02:10,023
through Fairlead, to a local model.

36
00:02:10,723 --> 00:02:15,245
Publish asks again,
then makes one commit on their branch.

37
00:02:15,245 --> 00:02:17,963
The review request asks again,

38
00:02:17,963 --> 00:02:21,496
then opens a pull request for the team.

39
00:02:22,246 --> 00:02:23,246
Now the trust check.

40
00:02:23,804 --> 00:02:25,749
A teammate pushes to the same branch.

41
00:02:26,449 --> 00:02:28,400
Gangplank sees it on refresh and stops:
saving stays off until they

42
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:29,400
get the latest.

43
00:02:29,543 --> 00:02:32,212
It never force-updates.

44
00:02:32,853 --> 00:02:35,385
The review request is listed for the team.

45
00:02:35,385 --> 00:02:38,560
Every write is in the audit log:
the branch, the commit, the review,

46
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:40,503
when and where, never contents or tokens.

47
00:02:41,203 --> 00:02:47,144
And the model call is on Fairlead's own
log: client Gangplank, local route,

48
00:02:47,144 --> 00:02:49,552
served by a small local model.

49
00:02:50,173 --> 00:02:53,765
That was Gangplank in test mode:
a synthetic GitHub,

50
00:02:53,765 --> 00:02:57,990
a live local model through Fairlead,
and the real safeguards.

51
00:02:57,990 --> 00:03:00,116
Its own branch, its own review.

52
00:03:00,116 --> 00:03:01,116
Fair winds.
